// COVERS DataSpaceLexerGrammar: DataSpace, executionContexts, defaultExecutionContext, name, mapping, defaultRuntime, supportInfo, Email, address, documentationUrl
//
// The other arm of `supportInfo:`. The rule is
//     supportInfo: SUPPORT_INFO COLON (supportEmail | supportCombinedInfo) SEMI_COLON
// -- exactly one alternative, so `Email` and `Combined` cannot share a DataSpace and the
// split into two fixtures is forced by the grammar, not by taste.
//
// `documentationUrl` is legal in BOTH arms (supportDocumentationUrl is listed inside
// supportEmail and supportCombinedInfo); it is written here as well as in t2-dataspace.pure
// so the Email arm is exercised in full rather than reduced to its one unique field.
//
// `address` is REQUIRED once `Email` is chosen -- DataSpaceParseTreeWalker.java:425 --
// which is why this element cannot be trimmed further.
###DataSpace
DataSpace fixture::ds::EmailSupported
{
  executionContexts:
  [
    {
      name: 'Context 1';
      mapping: fixture::ds::Mapping;
      defaultRuntime: fixture::ds::Runtime;
    }
  ];
  defaultExecutionContext: 'Context 1';
  supportInfo: Email {
    documentationUrl: 'https://example.org/docs';
    address: 'support@example.org';
  };
}
